<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The control panel's height, stated once.

      Every row in controls_panel.xml is a fixed height, so this is arithmetic
      and not a guess: 48dp icon row + 4dp padding, 44dp chord row, 48dp control
      row + 4dp, 48dp scroll row + 4dp = 200dp.

      It is stated rather than left to wrap_content because wrap_content did not
      hold. Measured on the SM-G970U: the rows need 600px and the panel was
      given 490, so the bottom row was drawn past the window edge and clipped to
      40px — first the control row, unnoticed for weeks because a short button
      still looks like a button, and then the scroll buttons, which is what made
      it visible. Two root layouts were tried, LinearLayout with a weight and
      RelativeLayout with the panel anchored to the bottom, and both produced
      the same 490.

      2026-09-18: THE ARITHMETIC ABOVE WAS SHORT. It never counted the chord
      row's padding: on a 440dpi screen the rows need 557px and 200dp is 550, so
      the last row — the scroll pair, the operator's only way to scroll — was
      clipped first, and the operator reported it missing. Upright, the panel is
      now re-measured after every layout (MainActivity.fitPortraitPanel), so this
      figure is only the first frame's estimate; ScrollPairOnScreenTest asserts
      the pair is whole, upright and sideways, and when a row above it grows.
    -->
    <dimen name="controls_panel_height">204dp</dimen>

    <!--
      How wide the control column is when the phone is held sideways.

      200dp. It was 340dp, which is what ENABLE + CONNECT + DISCONNECT +
      Settings measure on one line — and a column can be no narrower than its
      widest row. The operator's verdict on that: *"when i turn it sideways the
      button pannel takes 50% of the screen (entire right side)"*.

      `reflowPanel` gives the two crowded rows a second line in landscape, which
      is what lets this be 200dp: about 28% of the screen rather than half, and
      no label is clipped to get it.
    -->
    <dimen name="controls_panel_width">200dp</dimen>
</resources>
